lmbs[i].aa_index = be32_to_cpu(lmbs[i].aa_index);
```
```c
lmbs[i].aa_index = cpu_to_be32(lmbs[i].aa_index);
```
Reason:
These statements ensure that the `aa_index` is correctly converted to and from the appropriate endianness (CPU endian-ness and big-endian) when adding or removing memory. This fix aligns the `aa_index` with the other properties, preventing issues with node retrieval and ensuring the correct nodes are used in the code.


